<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>Sources and credits</title><style>@font-face{font-family:Lato;src:url(lato2-regular.woff)}@font-face{font-family:Lato;src:url(lato2-bold.woff);font-weight:700}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{font:18px/1.6 Lato,Arial,sans-serif;color:#34383c;background:#f3f5f8;margin:0}header{background:#24265f;color:white;padding:32px max(24px,calc((100vw - 1000px)/2))}header img{width:150px;height:60px;object-fit:contain;object-position:left}h1{font-size:36px;line-height:1.18;margin:20px 0 14px}h2{font-size:25px;color:#343895;line-height:1.3}h3{font-size:20px}main{max-width:1050px;margin:36px auto;padding:0 24px 50px}article,section.card{background:white;border:1px solid #dbe1e8;border-radius:14px;padding:28px;margin:24px 0}a{color:#343895;text-underline-offset:3px}a:hover{color:#527b20}p{margin:12px 0}nav{display:flex;gap:15px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:18px 0}.badge{background:#8DC63F;color:#192048;border-radius:50px;padding:5px 12px;font-size:13px;font-weight:700;display:inline-block}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;margin:20px 0}th,td{padding:12px;border:1px solid #cbd1d9;text-align:left;vertical-align:top}th{background:#eef2f7}li{margin:9px 0}.answer{min-height:95px;border:1px solid #aeb9c6;border-radius:5px;padding:12px;white-space:pre-wrap}.muted{color:#69727d;font-size:15px}button,.button{background:#343895;color:white;border:0;border-radius:7px;padding:10px 17px;font:inherit;text-decoration:none;cursor:pointer}button:focus-visible,a:focus-visible,[contenteditable]:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #8DC63F;outline-offset:4px}.compact{font-size:16px}@media(max-width:600px){body{font-size:16px}h1{font-size:29px}article,section.card{padding:20px}th,td{padding:8px;font-size:14px}table{display:block;overflow:auto}}@media print{header{background:white;color:#343895;padding:0}header img,nav,button{display:none}body{background:white;font-size:11pt}main{max-width:none;margin:0;padding:0}article,section.card{break-inside:avoid;border:0;padding:0;margin:22px 0}.answer{min-height:90px}h1{font-size:22pt}}</style></head><body><header><img src="../ocp_academy_white.svg" alt="OCP Academy"><h1>Sources and credits</h1><p>LVDC Power Distribution for Data Centers</p></header><main><article><h2>Primary source</h2><p><strong>Open Compute Project, DCF Power Distribution LVDC white paper, version 1.1.0, 2 September 2026.</strong> Teaching-slide citations use the one-based PDF page numbers, which match the printed page numbers in the supplied paper.</p><nav><a href="https://www.opencompute.org/documents/dcf-power-distribution-lvdc-white-paper-version-1-1-0-pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Official document link</a><a href="lvdc_whitepaper_v1_1_0.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open bundled paper</a></nav><p>The page pills open the bundled paper at the cited page, preserving the reviewed version. Browser PDF support determines whether the page anchor is honored; the full page range remains visible on each pill.</p></article><article><h2>Public presentation</h2><p>The 2026 OCP EMEA Summit presentation on LVDC power distribution provides public project context. The version 1.1.0 paper remains the primary technical baseline.</p><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=B0DhexBIaTo" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Watch the public EMEA Summit presentation</a></article><article><h2>Current document-status examples</h2><p>Official status checked during course preparation on 25 September 2026. Check current status and applicability for an actual project.</p><ul><li><a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://webstore.iec.ch/en/publication/67514">IEC 60947-10:2026</a>: published International Standard, 12 May 2026, for semiconductor circuit-breakers within its stated scope.</li><li><a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://www.ul.com/insights/path-safety-and-quality-solid-state-circuit-breakers">UL Solutions: solid-state circuit-breakers</a>: explains UL 489I as an Outline of Investigation.</li><li><a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://webstore.iec.ch/en/publication/72877">IEC 60038 catalog record</a>: use the current catalog to distinguish published voltage requirements from amendment proposals.</li></ul></article><article><h2>Figures and attribution</h2><p>The rack-entry illustration in Module 6, slide 3 is Figure 9.1 from the OCP paper, p. 166. It is cropped to the figure, with surrounding prose and the original caption removed. The course supplies its own explanatory caption.</p><p>Other diagrams and animations are original conceptual teaching adaptations of the paper sections cited on their slides. They simplify relationships and do not assign engineering ratings or unresolved numerical requirements. The Module 10 scenario is fictional.</p><p>The paper and its covered materials are made available under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0</a> (paper p. 238). The teaching adaptations are shared under the same license. OCP branding remains the property of its respective owner.</p></article><nav><a href="related_training.html">Related Academy training</a><a href="review_worksheet.html">Review worksheet</a></nav></main></body></html>